					"type": "MainSpriteFont",
					"properties": {
						"text": "[color=E25A12]Alex:[/color]\n\n[color=989DB1]How do you start a given project? And please take me through your process of titling.[/color]\n\n[color=50A359]Sean:[/color]\n\n[color=989DB1]In the last two months or so, I don't use the [color=737995]Reset[/color] button often. I paint over my completed works because generating ideas from a used canvas are easier than an uninspiring wall of color. Using old, completed paintings also allows me to spend less time creating a brand new background. In terms of how I title my work, I think about names way too long. The title is either meant to be descriptive, or stupid. You don't see the unusual names.[/color]",
